      "writtenOn": "2020-11-24T20:40:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`failed_attempts` are already incremented in line 1170 \"per operation\".\n\n`failed_attempts` is intended to signify failure to enqueue packet in the EC FIFO.\nIncrementing for \"I2C transfer fail\" (to clear) may be double-counting, and not appropriate.\n\nThis is also a blind \"delete the TCPC FIFO message\" write. We assume success. Separate error handling. Please see line 1205. We don\u0027t check for failure there either.\n\nMessage alerts only populate the `alert` register, not the `extended` register.",
